<title>USA: Maine says lacks funds for capital transport needs.</title>
<headline>Maine says lacks funds for capital transport needs.</headline>
<dateline>AUGUSTA 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maine Transportation Commissioner John Melrose said the state will be short millions of dollars to meet capital needs, including bridge replacement and major road reconstruction.</p>
<p>The state official said the budget he has submitted has the revenue for continuing programs, but predicted finding the funds to make up the capital shortfall will be a major problem for the legislature.</p>
<p>Melrose explained the budget has inadequate funding for capital improvements partly because a lot of the state's bridges were built in a short time, and now need to be replaced.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
